# Protocol gaps and inconsistencies (steward)
Each is returned to the documents if they answer; otherwise it is the maintainer's. No position fills them in.

- G1 "smoke" is called a 档位 (tier) by OBJ, but I3 tiers are T0/T1/T2. `smoke` exists only as a tool profile in old CFG `tools.yaml` (generators → placeholder, runs unofficial). The result must be labelled unofficial/placeholder; no tier (T0/T1) result is claimed. Maintainer to confirm if a tier label is wanted.
- G2 `duration_s` basis (video stream vs container): documents silent. OBJ lets task-maker/auditor choose by comparison with `d509bed`, with reason; both bases reported. Not decided here.
- G3 Judge vendor rule: I3 §2.4 says the judge must be a different vendor from the system's base model; OBJ treats `fixed` as model-free so no conflict, but how to enforce in general is the maintainer's (open decision 4). `gemini-3.8-flash` stand-in is temporary per OBJ.
- G4 Number of runs for this round: I3 says 3 per task; OBJ says "一轮". Documents do not say how many for the smoke run. Executor should do what its package states and record it; maintainer to confirm if not 3.
- G5 Provenance thresholds and scene `kappa` appear only in old CFG, not in I3 text (I3 §2.5 says thresholds are set on the stress test, which is out of scope). Used as given in CFG, flagged "CFG only".
- G6 Per-measure formulas (F1 matching rule, WER normalisation, onset error aggregation, purity, scene order, duration weighting) and the Q pass thresholds beyond ±5% are not in I3; old implementation is reference only. Scorer must record the implementation used; any ambiguity returns here. Speaker/character consistency needs human speaker labels (I3 §2.7) — likely "未运行" for a dialogue-free film (0 lines).
- G7 OBJ says CrewCut Issue #13 holds the reference price table; it is not in the readable documents. Comparison cannot be made unless a neighbour supplies its content; otherwise "未运行".
- G8 Dev totals in I3 (598 tasks, 299 segments) are across six dev films; the objective's round covers one film (90 task IDs per I3 §1.6).

## Stage B additions (OBJ steward#8)
- G9 I3 §1.1 lists Coffee Run (3.1 min) with 5 shots, yet OBJ says it has 28 tasks; 5 shots is hard to reconcile with that (and with 3,584 shots over 598 tasks). Documents inconsistent; the comparison with `d509bed` decides what the dataset has. Not resolved here; task-maker/auditor report the observed count. Maintainer to confirm the I3 table figure.
- G10 Sherlock Jr. has `page: null` in CFG `films.yaml`: no source URL for fetching the pinned master (SHA-256 is given). Backup copy exists only for Caminandes 3. If curator cannot find a source whose file hashes to 8931dc7b..., the film cannot be admitted by the documents; the maintainer decides (provide a file or drop the film). Nothing is substituted.
- G11 T1 video generation: CFG says Wan 2.2 self-hosted (price per GPU-second); OBJ decision says Alibaba-hosted Wan 2.2. Price basis (per second of video vs GPU time) is not in the documents; task-maker takes it from the official page. The T1 model variant is not pinned beyond "Wan 2.2".
- G12 Price table: CFG `prices.yaml` has no model rows; CrewCut Issue #13 is not readable by positions (see G7). Prices for `claude-opus-5-5`, `gpt-6.1-sol`, `gemini-4-argon`, `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`, `qwen3-vl-plus` and the generators come from official pages (OBJ). Subscription systems are priced nominally and must be marked so.
- G13 Budget gate: OBJ says stop and report when estimate + spent would exceed USD 1,500, but does not say who computes the estimate. Proposed reading (not a protocol change): executor reports per-minute cost after Coffee Run per system, scorer/auditor cost report adds judge and VLM spend, steward raises the stop to the maintainer. Request counts: the 150 gemini request cap of stage A is not stated in OBJ #8; stage B request caps are those of the resources (see `ht-resource describe`).
- G14 Run counts: I3 §2.4 requires 3 runs per task (L4: 2); OBJ asks 1 per system per task this stage (extends G4). Results are single-run; no variance or leaderboard claim. Maintainer to confirm.
- G15 `smoke`/T1: OBJ says T1 is only smoked on the fixed pipeline; CFG `smoke` profile is placeholders and unofficial (G1). Whether that T1 smoke uses real Wan 2.2 or the placeholder is not stated; executor must label which.
- G16 OBJ order says per-batch audit and `hengworld publish`, while "不给 world 写回权限" and the outputs section say export only through `hengworld artifacts`. Read as: publish within the world = artifacts for outside upload. If the commands differ, the maintainer clarifies.
- G17 Sandbox model access for Claude Code/Codex depends on HuTian#326; any failure is to be documented as phenomenon (command, error, time stream) in `protocol/hutian-issue-material.md` (steward) from executor's records; no workaround.
